{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1408361-range-bands-to-concrete-distances","id":1408361,"title":"Range bands to concrete distances?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-15T08:31:55-07:00","id":1408361,"title":"Range bands to concrete distances?","content":"Has anyone tried running the game with range bands converted into actual distances? Ie, declaring that one range band is thirty feet, or fifty feet, or something to that effect? If so, how did it go? Any unexpected issues?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T09:28:33-07:00","id":1408368,"title":"","content":"Can't say I have, and I don't see the point. Exact footage is a pain in the ass to keep track of, and doesn't really add much to the game.<br /> <br /> It may be that i'm bad at estimating exact length, but &quot;Close range is immediate stabbing/punching range, Short is lunge-then-stab range&quot; clicks immediately for me in a way that numbers don't","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:35:17-07:00","id":1408377,"title":"","content":"You can approximate using the old ranges from 1/2E for weapons like Firewands and Bows compared to the new ranges. I sometimes use distances as fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:42:29-07:00","id":1408378,"title":"","content":"So, interestingly enough, I saw an explaination of range bands that makes a bit more sense to me and makes pinning them down to exact distances impossible.<br /> <br /> Basically the idea is that range bands are mutable and change depending on the environment and people involved. For example a bar brawl, everyone brawling over the tables is in Close range of one another, but the guy with the bow standing up a half flight of stairs is at Short range. He might only be ten feet away, but in the context of everyone else using fists and knives, and in the environment of a really enclosed space that\u2019s still a range band. Now if we\u2019re on a big open battlefield charging a fortress gate lots of people are mounted, most will be using long weapons like lances or naginata. At that point ten feet is still in Close range, where Short might be more like 30 feet. BUT what if the wall is only 20 feet high? Well, in that case the range band gets a bit squished, so it might be 30 feet horizontally, but 20 vertical, since it doesn\u2019t make any sense for people on the ground to treat them like they\u2019re in melee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-15T10:52:47-07:00","id":1408381,"title":"","content":"The first and biggest issue you have to resolve is that it\u2019s not a linear rationship; in terms of hard distances, medium &gt; 2*short and long &gt; 3*short, which means there\u2019s huge ramifications from how you convert character speeds vs. weapon ranges. Then once you\u2019ve decided how fast people are you have to figure out how the heck rush, disengage, and withdraw work, since they\u2019re all based on the premise that you can chase or flee from someone without necessarily or immediately changing your position on the battle map (if you\u2019re using one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-16T03:09:35-07:00","id":1408470,"title":"","content":"Yeah, going from medium to long range is a LOT more yards than going from close to short.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}